From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reilly Brogan <reilly@reillybrogan.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Fix libtool versioning to keep the libyaml-0.so.2 soname

The 0.2.6 release bumped YAML_AGE without bumping YAML_CURRENT, which
lowers the libtool soname from libyaml-0.so.2 to libyaml-0.so.1 and
breaks every existing consumer. The interface only gained symbols, so
per the algorithm documented in configure.ac this should be REVISION=0,
CURRENT+=1, AGE+=1.

Origin: vendor
Forwarded: https://github.com/yaml/libyaml/issues/374
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
---
 configure | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configure b/configure
index 8d97787..72d0908 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -3545,8 +3545,8 @@ printf "%s\n" "#define YAML_VERSION_STRING \"0.2.6\"" >>confdefs.h
 
 # Define substitutions for the libtool version numbers.
 YAML_LT_RELEASE=0
-YAML_LT_CURRENT=2
-YAML_LT_REVISION=10
+YAML_LT_CURRENT=3
+YAML_LT_REVISION=0
 YAML_LT_AGE=1
 
 
